  "history": "Founded in 2009 in New York by Joshua Kushner, then 24, with a $5M first fund seeded by General Catalyst's Joel Cutler, Thrive Capital became one of the defining growth investors of the 2010s and 2020s: an early backer of Instagram, Warby Parker, Kickstarter and GitHub, the co-founder and incubator of Oscar Health (2013), the lead of Stripe's 2014 Series C, Slack's 2016 Series F and Affirm's 2019 Series F, and since 2023 OpenAI's largest venture shareholder alongside positions in SpaceX, Databricks, Anduril and Cursor. Ten flagship funds (Fund X closed at $10B+ in February 2026, $1B early-stage and $9B growth) and $50.5B of regulatory assets under one registered adviser; Thrive Holdings (the AI buy-and-build holdco, spun out 2025) and Thrive Eternal (permanent capital for sports and cultural assets, 2026) sit outside the venture firm.",
